[Chapter "Two Knights (3...Nf6)"]
[Line "Against the early ...d5"]
[Opening "Italian Game: Two Knights Defense, Modern Bishop's Opening"]

{Black hits the centre at once. Take, then castle and target the d5 knight.} 1. e4 {Take the centre and open lines for the queen and the f1 bishop.} 1... e5 2. Nf3 {Develop with an attack on e5.} 2... Nc6 3. Bc4 {The Italian: the bishop aims at f7, the weakest square in Black's camp.} 3... Nf6 {Black counterattacks e4.} 4. d3 {Calm and solid: protect e4 and keep the game in Italian structures.} 4... d5 5. exd5 {Take: Black can't recapture with a pawn.} 5... Nxd5 6. O-O {Castle quickly. Re1 and Nc3 will put pressure on the d5 knight and the e5 pawn.} *
